abstract: >-
  Companion repository for a short algebraic note on the eigenvalue
  decomposition of the symmetric, trace-free strain-rate tensor of a
  divergence-free field, together with a Lean 4 formalization. Lean proves,
  with 0 sorry and only the axioms propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound,
  the eigenvalue ordering λ₁ ≤ λ₂ ≤ λ₃, the trace-sum identity, the signs
  λ₁ ≤ 0 ≤ λ₃, and the intermediate-eigenvalue representation of the
  quadratic form ξ·Sξ (Proposition 1.1). The note is strictly algebraic and
  pointwise; it does not prove Hypothesis B, and a time-integrable bound on
  the L^∞ strain norm would require further hypotheses that remain open.
  No claim is made about the Clay Navier–Stokes problem.
  A kernel check is not a PDE or physical proof.
